<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/con-fscacher> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "con/fscacher is a Python library providing a persistent, file-content-aware memoization cache. Functions decorated with @cache.memoize_path are re-executed only when the fingerprint (timestamps + size) of their file arguments changes — making it easy to cache expensive operations on large file trees without stale results. It is used internally by the DANDI client and other CON tools." .
<https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/ns/projects/con-fscacher> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/demo-research-information/unreleased/XYZProject> .
