_:rc658d771ddb2cfeccecfc7f7_n856a4d7af4754df8ae9a4a1dce7ad4cfb8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/short_name> .
_:rc658d771ddb2cfeccecfc7f7_n856a4d7af4754df8ae9a4a1dce7ad4cfb8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rc658d771ddb2cfeccecfc7f7_n856a4d7af4754df8ae9a4a1dce7ad4cfb8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "OpenNeuro" .
_:rc658d771ddb2cfeccecfc7f7_n856a4d7af4754df8ae9a4a1dce7ad4cfb9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/description_html> .
_:rc658d771ddb2cfeccecfc7f7_n856a4d7af4754df8ae9a4a1dce7ad4cfb9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rc658d771ddb2cfeccecfc7f7_n856a4d7af4754df8ae9a4a1dce7ad4cfb9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "<p> <a href=\"https://openneuro.org\">OpenNeuro</a> is likely the oldest and the most well known <a href=\"https://braininitiative.nih.gov/\">BRAIN Initiative</a> archive for neuroimaging data. One of the exciting features of the project is that being inspired by our early <a href=\"https://datasets.datalad.org/?dir=/openfmri\">DataLad crawling</a> of its <a href=\"https://openfmri.org/\">OpenfMRI.org</a> precursor, it is now using <a href=\"https://git-annex.branchable.com\">git-annex</a> directly as its core technology. CON is contributing in ensuring availability of recent versions of git-annex and DataLad, involved standardization efforts, and inter-archive collaborations. </p> <ul> <li> <a href=\"https://reporter.nih.gov/project-details/10881961\">NIH (#5R24MH117179-07)</a>. PI: <a href=\"https://profiles.stanford.edu/russell-poldrack\">R. Poldrack</a>, Co-I: <a href=\"/whoweare#yaroslav_o_halchenko_\" class=\"centroid\">Y.O. Halchenko</a> </li> <li> <a href=\"https://github.com/OpenNeuroStudies/OpenNeuroStudies\">OpenNeuroStudies</a>: a <a href=\"#datalad\">DataLad</a> superdataset organising OpenNeuro datasets into BIDS Study structure together with their derivatives. </li> </ul>" .
_:rc74d7ede5ffab77b40de80bd_n005833b4d13b4962bc84a1bbe48b2e14b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/name> .
_:rc74d7ede5ffab77b40de80bd_n005833b4d13b4962bc84a1bbe48b2e14b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://concepts.datalad.org/s/things/v2/AttributeSpecification> .
_:rc74d7ede5ffab77b40de80bd_n005833b4d13b4962bc84a1bbe48b2e14b1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "University of Texas at Austin" .
